@startuml
title Java — lifecycle event emission
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #425466
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
hide footbox
autonumber

actor Application as app
participant DefaultLifecycle as core #EDF5FF
participant "Atomic phase /\ncondition map" as state #EDF5FF
participant OpenTelemetryLifecycleSink as sink #EAF7EE
participant "OTel Logger / SDK" as sdk #FFF1D6
participant "SDK processors /\nexporter" as exporter #FFF1D6

app -> core : phase(...), milestone(...) or condition(...)
core -> core : Validate inputs; copy and normalize caller attributes
break Invalid input
  core --> app : Throw argument exception; no state change or event
end
opt Phase or condition (milestones are stateless)
  core -> state : Atomic update, including duplicate values
  state --> core : Previous value, or absent
end
core -> core : Read monotonic elapsed and wall clock\nCreate immutable LifecycleEvent
core -> sink : emit(event)
sink -> sdk : logRecordBuilder()\nsetEventName / setTimestamp / setBody\nsetSeverity(INFO) / typed attributes / emit()
sdk -> exporter : Pass record through configured processors
note over sdk, exporter
  Host Resource supplies identity; current trace context is inherited.
  A batch processor may defer export; a simple processor may export here.
end note
exporter --> sdk
sdk --> sink
sink --> core
core --> app : Return

note over core, sink
  If emit throws an ordinary exception, the core contains it and
  invokes its optional diagnostic callback. Observed state is retained.
  Composite sinks independently contain failures and attempt each child.
end note
note over app, exporter
  Calls are synchronous; concurrent deliveries may arrive out of order.
  Returning from the call is not a delivery acknowledgement.
end note
@enduml
